{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A cancel during the post-merge metadata read briefly reports cancellation before the record correctly returns to landed, because the PR has already merged."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A landed review round whose request closes the owner's issue is permanently recorded as superseded, which can mislead someone assessing its outcome."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"MCP approvals that omit the optional consumer are routinely attributed to a human, but the evidence identifies no runtime effect beyond incorrect provenance."}]}